<title>USA: Southern Natl, United Carolina merge.</title>
<headline>Southern Natl, United Carolina merge.</headline>
<dateline>WINSTON-SALEM, N.C. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern National Corp and United Carolina Bancshares Corp said on Monday their boards had approved a stock-swap merger valued at $985 million.</p>
<p>UCB shareholders will receive 1.135 shares of Southern National for each UCB share, they said.</p>
<p>The deal will be accounted for as a pooling of interests.</p>
<p>Based on Southern National's closing price on November 1 of $35.25, each UCB share would be worth $40.01 in the merger, the companies said.</p>
</text>
